title: Ignore presets
tags: [[File tracking]]
kind: reference
aliases: ignore ignores preset presets ignore-presets excluded
summary: Named groups of mf_ignore patterns in core/ignore-presets.toml, expanded by the client — the daemon only ever sees patterns.

A ''preset'' is a named, reusable group of `mf_ignore` patterns, in
`~/.config/metafolder/core/ignore-presets.toml` (installed with the configuration). It
exists for naming and grouping only: turning a preset into patterns is done by the
client (`core::ignore_presets`, shared by `mf` and the GUI) — the daemon never sees a
preset name, only the patterns written.

```
[rust-build]
description = "Cargo build intermediates (keeps the final binaries)"
patterns = ['(^|/)target/([^/]+/)?[^/]+/(deps|build|incremental|examples|\.fingerprint)(/.*)?$']

[default]
description = "The default set of mf_ignore patterns for a fresh root"
pattern-set = ["rust-build", "node", "node-build", "python", "julia", "cpp",
               "java", "cache", "os", "editor", "git", "metafolder", "hidden"]
```

A preset is a ''leaf'' (a `patterns` list), a ''group'' (a `pattern-set` of other
presets, expanded recursively), or both (the union). A reference cycle is an error, and
so is a missing or malformed file — pointing at `metafolder-sync-config`, never falling
back ([[No runtime fallback]]).

|!Preset |!Leaves out |
|`rust-build` |cargo's regenerated intermediates under `target/<profile>/` (`deps/`, `build/`, `incremental/`, `.fingerprint/`, `examples/`) — the final binaries stay tracked |
|`node`, `node-build` |`node_modules`; JS/TS build caches and compiled native addons |
|`python` |bytecode and tool caches |
|`julia` |coverage, build and doc output |
|`cpp` |object files, precompiled headers, CMake files |
|`java` |`.class` files and the Gradle cache |
|`cache` |generic caches and temporary files |
|`os` |`.DS_Store`, `Thumbs.db`… |
|`editor` |swap, backup and autosave files |
|`git`, `metafolder` |`.git`, `.metafolder` |
|`hidden` |every dot-prefixed entry |
|`default` |all of the above — what a new root gets |

The shipped set is ''conservative'': only clearly regenerable intermediates and junk,
never ambiguous names like `dist/` or `build/`, static libraries or extension-less
executables, which are often deliverables. `git` and `metafolder` stay separate from
`hidden` (which already covers them) so that dropping "all hidden entries" from a
directory does not silently un-ignore `.git` and `.metafolder`. Edit the file to add
your own presets; applying them: [[Setting ignore patterns]].
